From 0610d85cfa2bac949e94cb280a3ae9c3b12a753c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:32:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 80/90] feat(visualizer): give Hanabi a real settings panel

The parameters now live in the visualizer settings store like every other
style's, instead of being read ad hoc by the entry:

- store: hanabiTuning + handleSetHanabiTuning / handleResetHanabiTuning, with
  the same merge-then-normalise write path the other tunings use, persisted
  under hanabi_tuning
- hanabi/tuning.ts becomes a tuningRegistry adapter, so the render boundary
  injects props.hanabiTuning (and useVisualizerTunings now carries it - without
  that the bundle never had hanabi and the panel's changes went nowhere)
- HanabiSettingsPanel: six sections (look, lyrics, fireworks, sky & camera,
  bloom, quality) on the tempera RangeControl / SettingsSection /
  VisualizerPresetGroup primitives, plus reset. Upstream's version is built on
  the 0.7.21 settings kit; this one reads the store directly so neither
  SettingsModal nor VisPlayground needed new plumbing
- tuningDefinition.ts is gone: the tuning now goes through tuningRegistry, so
  the subset file that existed only for Hanabi has no user left

Verified on the device: the panel's segmented controls write colour mode and
render quality into hanabi_tuning, and textOnly set through it strips the sky,
fireworks and ornaments from the live picture while the lyrics stay.
